  "limitations": [
    "API-09 still owns the process-wide application/problem+json vocabulary, browser Origin and CSRF controls, and global timeout and retry policy. API-04 has a bounded transport wait, JSON-only input, operator authorization, safe fixed errors, and non-cacheable application responses but does not claim the complete API-09 boundary.",
    "Campaign-brief and demo-scenario registries are not implemented yet. The typed optional identifiers are retained in the transport contract, but every non-null value fails closed as an unregistered resource rather than inventing a revision or scenario.",
    "API-07 still owns the run-detail resource behind runUrl, while WEB-04 and DEL-07 own the schema-generated form, committed OpenAPI artifact, generated client, and drift gate. API-04 returns workId separately and does not emit a nonexistent workUrl.",
    "DEL-04 still owns database migrations and insert-only seed bootstrap, while DEL-05 owns runnable default startup and service composition. API-04 proves the real HTTP route, service, compiled resolver, and durable unit of work when dependency-injected into the application factory, but does not claim that the default process constructs them yet.",
    "The SQLite manual-admission unit of work obtains write intent before reading effective configuration and retries only bounded recognized lock conflicts; a deterministic one-millisecond-busy-timeout test proves simultaneous exact retries converge and changed submissions split into one creation and one conflict. Generic SQLite transactions and PostgreSQL behavior are unchanged; no live PostgreSQL service or optional PostgreSQL driver is required by this local gate."
  ]
